owing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T21:20:07Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T21:20:07Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2707481821/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711686393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103089#issuecomment-2711686393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103089","id":2711686393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hoQz5","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T20:00:21Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T20:01:21Z","body":"This increased our minimum requiredPython version to 3.9. We should update the docs accordingly and notify developers since this breaks pre-commit for everyone on older versions of Python.\r\n\r\nAlso, I question whether this was necessary in the first place. It wasn't fixing a bug or addressing any issue. It just creates work for everyone for no discernable gain. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711686393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711736317","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103089#issuecomment-2711736317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103089","id":2711736317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hoc_9","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T20:22:53Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T20:23:34Z","body":"> Also, I question whether this was necessary in the first place. It wasn't fixing a bug or addressing any issue. It just creates work for everyone for no discernable gain.\r\n\r\nKeeping dependencies up-to-date is a good idea in general. We do the same with thirdparty libraries. Those projects fix bugs, improve performance, and implement new features, which might have immediate or future benefits for us. Sometimes they also introduce bugs and by catching them early we can be good open source citizens and report them so they get fixed, or just roll back the changes.\r\n\r\nBut yes, we need to evaluate how such updates impact existing workflows, and here I believe the fact that mypy 1.50.0 dropped support for Python 3.8 was likely overlooked:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/python/mypy/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md#drop-support-for-python-38\r\n\r\nPython 3.8 is EOL so that's not unreasonable, but in this case since we don't *need* to update, I think we can stay on mypy 1.49.1 for the time-being, until we decide to drop Python 3.8 support.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711736317/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711802064","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103089#issuecomment-2711802064","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103089","id":2711802064,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hotDQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T20:54:58Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T20:54:58Z","body":"I think the most important thing is we need to flag for contributors when our minimum requirements change. \r\n\r\nIn this case pre commit was failing even after reinstalling with a long list of unrelated errors which made the important error hard to spot. Once I suspected that my python version was out of date I checked the docs and confirmed that 3.8 was fine still. Which made me circle around for a bit before reading through the mypy release notes. \r\n\r\nTo be clear, I agree with keeping dependencies reasonably up to date. But we do need to put more thought into incrementing versions when they increase minimum requirements. At the very least we need to keep our docs up to date, but we should also be willing to delay updating to minimize the number of times we break compatibility ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711802064/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711818288","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103089#issuecomment-2711818288","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103089","id":2711818288,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hoxAw","user":{"login":"Chubercik","id":37378746,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3Mzc4NzQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37378746?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik","html_url":"https://github.com/Chubercik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T21:01:59Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T21:01:59Z","body":"> Python 3.8 is EOL so that's not unreasonable, but in this case since we don't _need_ to update, I think we can stay on mypy 1.49.1 for the time-being, until we decide to drop Python 3.8 support.\r\n\r\nAnd Python 3.9 will reach EOL in ~7 months time, I think using a supported version is in and of itself a worthwhile endeavor - so much so that I'd say to go for oldest supported version +1 (3.10 right now), so that when support for 3.9 is dropped we still have a year to move to 3.11.\r\n\r\nI must admit I missed the needed version bump because I've been on py 3.9 for, I guess, around 4 years now. I'll look into updating the docs asap.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711818288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711868162","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103089#issuecomment-2711868162","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103089","id":2711868162,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ho9MC","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T21:20:12Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T21:20:56Z","body":"@Chubercik I don't think we should force people to update Python version unless we have a very good reason to.\r\n\r\nManaging Python versions on all OSes is a nightmare, and in particular on Windows (which is the most likely platform for people to run into issues, because it doesn't auto-update and installing a new version just messes up the PATH and all tools currently using Python in my experience). So it's expected that some users might not want to touch their Python setup unless they really need to - including EOL which they might not care about.\r\n\r\nSo I would really just revert mypy to 0.14.1 and put a comment that we should stick to a version compatible with recently EOL'ed Python.\r\n\r\nFor example our ruff config targets Python 3.8. And SCons itself in its brand new 4.9.0 release just upped the min supported version to Python 3.7. So I would say 3.7 is our baseline, and 3.8 is a reasonable min to expect as it was just freshly EOL'ed and is likely still used by many.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711868162/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711887334","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103089#issuecomment-2711887334","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103089","id":2711887334,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hpB3m","user":{"login":"Chubercik","id":37378746,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3Mzc4NzQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37378746?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik","html_url":"https://github.com/Chubercik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T21:29:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T21:29:45Z","body":"Fair enough. I'm gonna trust your expertise on that one.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711887334/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]